{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT CAUSE (confirmed 2026-11-10 PST, session 3d705fec, worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-dore)\n\nThe test's readiness wait `_await_probe` had a fixed 3.0 s wall-clock ceiling. That ceiling covered the reconciler's startup work before `review_and_vote`: DedupStore SQLite WAL setup and `clear_voted` on the loop thread, the cursor read, and 2 executor hops. On a loaded runner that work can outlast 3 s. The failure message then blamed an unwired probe for what was only a slow start. The production shutdown drain was never exercised and is not implicated.\n\nEvidence:\n- CI's failure signature (run 42742825985, gw3): the 3.0 s message, NO captured stdout/stderr/log, and the test is absent from `--durations=25`, whose cutoff is 7.91 s. In-flight work would have triggered the 5 s drain (at least 8 s in total), so nothing was in flight. That rules out a review blocked inside `review_and_vote`, such as on a leaked per-change lock.\n- Fault injection, one change at a time:\n  - A 3.5 s stall in `reconcile._read_cursor` reproduces CI's exact signature: same message, no captured sections, 3.51 s call.\n  - A 2.5 s stall passes.\n  - Ruled out, because their signatures differ: a low-disk refusal (WARNING `REVIEW_RETRY_DEFERRED` captured), `compose_startup_binding` raising (a different error), and a stall inside `review_and_vote` (the drain runs the review, so the adapter WARNING is captured).\n- The same CI worker gw3 recorded a 6.36 s fixture setup in the same run, so stalls over 3 s did occur there.\n- No lock or in-flight leak across 142 review-bot tests in file order. 0 of 40 repeats failed under xdist on a host with load average 42.\n\nCorrection to the description: run 41638314556 did NOT fail this test. It logged only a `[rebar-ci-timing]` slow-fixture warning, on Windows. There is 1 confirmed failure. The Errno 98 is from `test_audit_serve::test_await_listening_reports_a_server_that_cannot_bind`, which binds a busy port on purpose; it is unrelated.\n\nFIX (the class, per the wall-clock policy in scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py): `_await_probe`'s cap becomes a 20 s hang-guard, shared by all 9 call sites. The wait returns as soon as the probe fires, so passing runs get no slower. The message no longer claims \"the probe is not wired\". The two reconciler-shutdown tests' outer `wait_for` rises from 20 s to 60 s so it stays above the cap plus the drain. Verified after the fix: the 3.5 s and 8 s injected stalls pass, test_review_bot.py and the wall-clock lint pass (151 passed), and wall-clock-asserts reports clean."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794363207240340968,"uuid":"9b8aab4f-673c-489e-9613-ba2f33211d8c"}